  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "2002 (Jan. - Feb.) U.S. Bottom Trawl Survey Leg 2 Data for Arrowtooth Flounder on the Outter Continental Shelf and Upper Slope of the Gulf of Alaska West of Kodiak Island - R/V Miller Freeman (Cruise ID: MF2002-01)",
  "description": "The Alaska Fisheries Science Center FOCI program conducted a bottom trawl survey on the outer continental shelf and upper slope of the Gulf of Alaska west of Kodiak Island. Bottom trawls were conducted to collect juvenile walleye pollock for otoliths and adult arrowtooth flounder for sexual maturity and spawning studies. Arrowtooth flounder data include lengths, otoliths, maturities, and gonads. Data (CTD) on physical characteristics of water in the area were also collected. Other collected samples include Cholorophyll, nutrient, microzooplankton, sebastes, bathymasterid larvae, capelin rough count, and quantitative tows preserved in formalin. Zooplankton data and data on physical characteristics of the water column were also be collected. Cruise ID: MF2002-01 (29 Jan. - 9 Feb. 2002) Survey vessels: R/V Miller Freeman For preliminary survey results see http://www.afsc.noaa.gov/race/surveys/cruise_archives/cruises2002/results_MF2002-01.pdf\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To conduct bottom trawl sampling on the outer continental shelf and upper slope in the Gulf of Alaska west of Kodiak Island in order to establish the apprearance of arrowtooth flounder eggs in the plankton.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23628973",
